#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""The flights of the game's flight masters and the ways of its boats and zeppelins, from its client tables, as
staging for Core's set Travel (pack World): the ways Navigation's route planner takes (Doc/ideas/Navigation.md,
*The planner*).

  dev/data/staging/travel.jsonl   one line per way, its key the game's TaxiPath ID:

    a flight      kind flight, fromNode and toNode (the game's flight points, as C_TaxiMap names them), side
                  (alliance or horde where only that side's flight masters stand at both ends; none: both), cost
                  (copper), length (yards along the game's path) and path (its points in the world's yards, x to
                  the north and y to the west)
    the tram      the Deeprun Tram (no taxi path moves it): kind tram, name (its map's, the game's), path (its two
                  stations in its map's yards: the game's triggers there, where one leaves it, each with its map),
                  length (yards between them), time (seconds a run from one to the other takes, as its cars move
                  in the game's TransportAnimation, the same for every car within AGREE seconds), wait (seconds
                  between two trains leaving one station: its cars' motion once round, the same for every car,
                  over the trains: its cars set out from their stations together, one train each way), docks and
                  dockAreas (the cities' entrances to each station, placed as a transport's docks), side (as a
                  transport's, by the flight masters near its entrances)
    a transport   a boat or a zeppelin, one way round as the game moves it (a path between no flight points): kind
                  (a boat when all its way lies within FLOAT yards of the sea's level, else a zeppelin), length
                  (yards it moves along its way once round, its leaps not counted) and path: its points, each with
                  map (the world's map it lies on, at its first point and wherever the way comes onto another),
                  stay (where it stops at a dock: the seconds it stands there, the game's delay) and jump (where it
                  leaps to the point from the one before, onto another map or far on the same: the game's teleport;
                  after its last point it starts again from its first), side (alliance or horde where its docks
                  lie near that side's flight masters alone, within DOCKSIDE yards: its towns'; none: both, as the
                  goblins' ports), docks (its docks on the zone maps, for the
                  map's pins: one per place it stops at, in the order it first comes to them, each placed by
                  map-data's Placer; a dock on no zone map left out) and dockAreas (the game's area each of them
                  lies in, the AreaTable ID its terrain or building gives, which names it; 0 where none does)
    a portal      with --portals (below): a trigger of the game's that brings one elsewhere on its continent the
                  moment one steps into it: kind portal, path (its two ends in the world's yards, each with z: the
                  trigger's place, the game's, with its map; then where it brings one), length (the yards between
                  them), from and to (the two on the zone maps, each placed by map-data's Placer, for the map's pins);
                  its key our own number, PORTALS + the trigger's ID
    a lift        with --lifts (below): a car that goes straight up and down, as the game moves it in its
                  TransportAnimation (no taxi path): kind lift, path (its two ends in the world's yards, the lower
                  first with its map, each with z, its height: where the car stands at the start of its motion,
                  moved to its motion's lowest and highest), length (the yards it rises), time (seconds from leaving
                  one end to reaching the other, the slower of its two rides), wait (seconds between two departures
                  from one end: its motion once round) and from and to (its lower and upper end on the zone maps,
                  each placed by map-data's Placer, for the map's pins); its key our own number, from LIFTS + 1 on,
                  that of the master's lift whose lower end lies within HERE yards where there is one

On a path a point on a straight run, within STRAIGHT yards of the line between its neighbours, is left out (never a
dock or a leap). The game's tables hold neither a transport's speed nor its timetable: the planner estimates them
until they are learned in play (Doc/ideas/Data.md, learned data).

The lifts' places are not in the client's tables: --lifts <places> <batch> takes them from a batch of our picking
(assets/data/sources.toml), a CSV file with a line per car (object, continent, x, y, z: the game object whose motion
TransportAnimation holds, the world's map it stands on, and where it stands at the start of its motion, in the
world's yards), and writes its lifts as that batch's lines. A car the client does not move as a lift (straight up and
down within STILL yards, standing once a round at each end of its way, within END yards of it, and nowhere between,
rising RISE yards or more) is left out.

Where a portal brings one is not in the client's tables either: --portals <places> <batch> takes it from a batch of our
picking, a CSV file with a line per portal (trigger, continent, x, y, z: the game's area trigger and where it brings
one, in the world's yards), and writes its portals as that batch's lines; a trigger the client does not have, or has on
another continent, is left out.

Left out: flights between flight points of no side (the game's own, not a flight master's); paths that stop at
fewer than two docks (a moving thing, no way between places); and a transport whose every dock is one of another
transport with more docks (or, with the same ones, a newer ID): the older way the newer one replaced. Two stops
within SAME yards on one map are one dock.

The input, of the build BUILD: a folder of the game's client tables as CSV (TaxiNodes, TaxiPath, TaxiPathNode,
AreaTrigger, Map and TransportAnimation for the tram and the lifts, and
for placing the docks those map-data reads: AreaTable, UiMap, UiMapAssignment, WMOAreaTable), and its terrain files
as map-data takes them.

Usage:  dev/tools/travel-data <client tables> <terrain> [--lifts <places> <batch>] [--portals <places> <batch>]
"""
import csv
import json
import math
import sys
from importlib.machinery import SourceFileLoader
from importlib.util import module_from_spec, spec_from_loader
from pathlib import Path

ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]
STAGING = ROOT / "dev" / "data" / "staging" / "travel.jsonl"
MASTER = ROOT / "assets" / "data" / "Travel" / "Travel.jsonl"
BUILD = 70245
STRAIGHT = 2.0  # yards
FLOAT = 5.0  # yards over or under the sea's level (0) a boat's way keeps to
SAME = 20.0  # yards between two stops of one dock
AGREE = 0.005  # seconds the tram's cars' runs may differ by
LIFTS = 1100000  # our own numbers of the lifts: from LIFTS + 1 on (the tram's, 1000369, lies below)
HERE = 5.0  # yards between a lift's lower end and that of the master's lift whose key it keeps
PORTALS = 1200000  # our own numbers of the portals: PORTALS + the game's area trigger ID
STILL = 1.0  # yards a lift's car may move sideways
END = 0.1  # yards from the end of its way within which a lift's car stands there
RISE = 10.0  # yards a lift rises at least (a door the game moves so rises less)
ALLIANCE, HORDE = 0x1, 0x2  # the flight points' sides in TaxiNodes' Flags
DOCKSIDE = 600.0  # yards from a dock within which one side's flight masters alone make it that side's town
TELEPORT, STOP = 0x1, 0x2  # TaxiPathNode's Flags: the transport leaps after this point; it stops here


def table(folder, name):
    return list(csv.DictReader(open(folder / f"{name}.csv", encoding="utf-8")))


def map_data():
    """dev/tools/map-data, whose Placer puts a world position on its zone map, read without running the tool."""
    loader = SourceFileLoader("map_data", str(ROOT / "dev" / "tools" / "map-data"))
    module = module_from_spec(spec_from_loader("map_data", loader))
    loader.exec_module(module)
    return module


def simplified(points):
    """The path's points (x and y first), those on a straight run left out (Douglas and Peucker)."""
    if len(points) < 3:
        return points
    a, b = points[0], points[-1]
    dx, dy = b[0] - a[0], b[1] - a[1]
    length = math.hypot(dx, dy)
    far, at = 0.0, 0
    for index in range(1, len(points) - 1):
        p = points[index]
        if length == 0:
            gap = math.hypot(p[0] - a[0], p[1] - a[1])
        else:
            gap = abs(dy * (p[0] - a[0]) - dx * (p[1] - a[1])) / length
        if gap > far:
            far, at = gap, index
    if far <= STRAIGHT:
        return [a, b]
    return simplified(points[:at + 1])[:-1] + simplified(points[at:])


def flight(key, row, a, b, path):
    """A flight's fields, or None when no flight master's side stands at both ends."""
    sides = [int(node["Flags"]) & (ALLIANCE | HORDE) for node in (a, b)]
    both = sides[0] & sides[1]
    if not all(sides) or not both:
        return None
    side = None if both == ALLIANCE | HORDE else ("alliance" if both == ALLIANCE else "horde")
    continent = int(a["ContinentID"])
    way = [(float(p["Loc[0]"]), float(p["Loc[1]"])) for p in path if int(p["ContinentID"]) == continent]
    length = sum(math.hypot(q[0] - p[0], q[1] - p[1]) for p, q in zip(way, way[1:]))
    fields = {"kind": "flight", "fromNode": int(row["FromTaxiNode"]), "toNode": int(row["ToTaxiNode"]),
              "cost": int(row["Cost"])}
    if len(way) >= 2:  # a way the game has no points for keeps no length nor path
        fields["length"] = round(length, 1)
        fields["path"] = [{"x": x, "y": y} for x, y in simplified(way)]
    if side:
        fields["side"] = side
    return fields


def docks(path):
    """A transport's docks: [(map, x, y, z)], one per place it stops at, where it first stops there."""
    found = []
    for p in path:
        if int(p["Flags"]) & STOP:
            place = (int(p["ContinentID"]), float(p["Loc[0]"]), float(p["Loc[1]"]), float(p["Loc[2]"]))
            if not any(d[0] == place[0] and math.hypot(d[1] - place[1], d[2] - place[2]) <= SAME for d in found):
                found.append(place)
    return found


def replaced(places):
    """The transports (by key: their docks) all of whose docks another one has, with more docks, or with the same
    ones and a newer ID: the older ways the newer ones replaced."""
    def within(small, large):
        return all(any(a[0] == b[0] and math.hypot(a[1] - b[1], a[2] - b[2]) <= SAME for b in large) for a in small)

    return {key for key in places for other in places if other != key and within(places[key], places[other])
            and (len(places[other]) > len(places[key]) or (len(places[other]) == len(places[key]) and other > key))}


def side(places, nodes):
    """A way's side from its docks ([(world, x, y, ...)]) and the flight points (nodes: {ID: its TaxiNodes row}):
    alliance or horde where a dock lies within DOCKSIDE yards of that side's flight masters alone (that side's town:
    its guards are the server's, its flight masters the client's) and none so near the other's alone; None else (a
    goblin port with both, no flight master near, or towns of both sides)."""
    towns = set()
    for world, x, y, *_ in places:
        near = 0
        for node in nodes.values():
            if int(node["ContinentID"]) == world and math.hypot(float(node["Pos[0]"]) - x,
                                                                float(node["Pos[1]"]) - y) <= DOCKSIDE:
                near |= int(node["Flags"]) & (ALLIANCE | HORDE)
        if near in (ALLIANCE, HORDE):
            towns.add(near)
    if len(towns) != 1:
        return None
    return "alliance" if towns == {ALLIANCE} else "horde"


def transport(path, placer=None, nodes=None):
    """A transport's fields from its path's points (in the game's order); its docks on the zone maps where a placer
    (map-data's Placer) is given; its side where the flight points are (nodes, side)."""
    points, length = [], 0.0
    for index, p in enumerate(path):
        world, x, y = int(p["ContinentID"]), float(p["Loc[0]"]), float(p["Loc[1]"])
        before = path[index - 1] if index else None
        leap = before is not None and (int(before["ContinentID"]) != world or int(before["Flags"]) & TELEPORT)
        if before is not None and not leap:
            length += math.hypot(x - float(before["Loc[0]"]), y - float(before["Loc[1]"]))
        point = {"x": x, "y": y}
        if before is None or int(before["ContinentID"]) != world:
            point["map"] = world
        if int(p["Flags"]) & STOP:
            point["stay"] = int(p["Delay"])
        if leap:
            point["jump"] = True
        points.append(point)
    # Straight runs left out between the points that must stay: the ends, the docks and the leaps (with the point
    # before each leap, where the transport leaves).
    kept = {0, len(points) - 1}
    for index, point in enumerate(points):
        if "stay" in point or "jump" in point:
            kept.add(index)
            if "jump" in point:
                kept.add(index - 1)
    marks = sorted(kept)
    out = []
    for start, end in zip(marks, marks[1:]):
        run = [(p["x"], p["y"], p) for p in points[start:end + 1]]
        if "jump" in points[end]:
            out.append(points[start])
            continue
        out += [p for _, _, p in simplified(run)][:-1]
    out.append(points[-1])
    heights = [abs(float(p["Loc[2]"])) for p in path]
    fields = {"kind": "boat" if max(heights) <= FLOAT else "zeppelin", "length": round(length, 1), "path": out}
    sided = nodes and side(docks(path), nodes)
    if sided:
        fields["side"] = sided
    if placer:
        placed = [(placer.place(*dock), placer.area(*dock)) for dock in docks(path)]
        placed = [(point, area) for point, area in placed if point]
        if placed:
            fields["docks"] = [point for point, _ in placed]
            fields["dockAreas"] = [area for _, area in placed]
    return fields


# The Deeprun Tram, by the game's IDs: its map; its two stations, each the trigger in that map where one leaves
# the tram and the trigger in the city that leads to it (AreaTrigger); its cars (TransportAnimation); and our own
# number for it in the set (the game has no path for it).
TRAM_MAP = 369
TRAM_STATIONS = ((2166, 2175), (2171, 2173))
TRAM_CARS = range(176080, 176086)
TRAM_KEY = 1000369


def tram(folder, placer=None, nodes=None):
    """The tram's fields, or None when the tables do not have it whole (a station, a car) or its cars disagree; its
    side where the flight points are (nodes, side: the cities' entrances to it)."""
    triggers = {int(row["ID"]): row for row in table(folder, "AreaTrigger")}
    if any(a not in triggers or b not in triggers for a, b in TRAM_STATIONS):
        return None
    moves = {}
    for row in table(folder, "TransportAnimation"):
        car = int(row["TransportID"])
        if car in TRAM_CARS:
            moves.setdefault(car, set()).add((int(row["TimeIndex"]), float(row["Pos[0]"]), float(row["Pos[1]"])))
    runs, rounds, ways = [], [], set()
    for car in TRAM_CARS:
        rows = sorted(moves.get(car, ()))
        if not rows:
            return None
        far = max(math.hypot(x, y) for _, x, y in rows)
        there = [t for t, x, y in rows if far - math.hypot(x, y) < 0.01]
        home = [t for t, x, y in rows if math.hypot(x, y) < 0.01 and t < there[0]]
        if not home:
            return None
        runs.append((there[0] - max(home)) / 1000)
        # Its motion once round (its last point, where the game starts it again), and which way it sets out.
        rounds.append(rows[-1][0] / 1000)
        x, y = next((x, y) for t, x, y in rows if t == there[0])
        ways.add((round(x / far), round(y / far)))
    if max(runs) - min(runs) > AGREE or max(rounds) - min(rounds) > AGREE:
        return None
    path, places = [], []
    for station, entrance in TRAM_STATIONS:
        here, door = triggers[station], triggers[entrance]
        if int(here["ContinentID"]) != TRAM_MAP:
            return None
        point = {"x": float(here["Pos[0]"]), "y": float(here["Pos[1]"])}
        if not path:
            point["map"] = TRAM_MAP
        path.append(point)
        places.append((int(door["ContinentID"]), float(door["Pos[0]"]), float(door["Pos[1]"]), float(door["Pos[2]"])))
    name = next((row["MapName_lang"] for row in table(folder, "Map") if int(row["ID"]) == TRAM_MAP), "")
    fields = {"kind": "tram", "length": round(math.hypot(path[1]["x"] - path[0]["x"], path[1]["y"] - path[0]["y"]), 1),
              "time": sorted(runs)[len(runs) // 2], "path": path}
    # A train each way, each from its own station at the round's start: each station sees a train leave twice a round.
    if len(ways) == 2:
        fields["wait"] = round(sorted(rounds)[len(rounds) // 2] / len(ways), 3)
    if name:
        fields["name"] = name
    sided = nodes and side(places, nodes)
    if sided:
        fields["side"] = sided
    if placer:
        placed = [(placer.place(*door), placer.area(*door)) for door in places]
        if all(point for point, _ in placed):
            fields["docks"] = [point for point, _ in placed]
            fields["dockAreas"] = [area for _, area in placed]
    return fields


def lift(rows):
    """A lift's motion from its car's TransportAnimation rows (TimeIndex in milliseconds, Pos its offset from where it
    stands at the start): (low, high, time, wait), its lowest and highest height from there, the seconds of the slower
    of its two rides and of its motion once round; None for a motion that is no lift's."""
    keys = sorted((int(row["TimeIndex"]), float(row["Pos[0]"]), float(row["Pos[1]"]), float(row["Pos[2]"]))
                  for row in rows)
    if len(keys) < 3 or keys[0][0] != 0 or any(abs(x) > STILL or abs(y) > STILL for _, x, y, _ in keys):
        return None
    low, high = min(key[3] for key in keys), max(key[3] for key in keys)
    whole = keys[-1][0]  # once round: at its last keyframe it starts again from its first
    if high - low < RISE or whole <= 0:
        return None
    # Each keyframe of a round, a ring: at its lowest (-1), at its highest (1), or between (0); one standing between
    # its ends (two keyframes alike there) stops at a floor between them: no lift of two ends.
    ring = [(t, -1 if z - low <= END else 1 if high - z <= END else 0) for t, _, _, z in keys[:-1]]
    if any(ring[index][1] == 0 and abs(keys[index][3] - keys[index + 1][3]) <= END for index in range(len(ring))):
        return None
    start = next((index for index in range(len(ring)) if ring[index][1] != ring[index - 1][1]), None)
    if start is None:
        return None
    # The runs of keyframes alike, around the ring from a change on, so that none is cut in two.
    runs = []
    for step in range(len(ring)):
        index = (start + step) % len(ring)
        when, mark = ring[index][0] + (whole if index < start else 0), ring[index][1]
        if runs and runs[-1][0] == mark:
            runs[-1][2] = when
        else:
            runs.append([mark, when, when])
    stands = [run for run in runs if run[0]]
    if sorted(run[0] for run in stands) != [-1, 1]:
        return None  # it stands more than once at an end, or never: no lift's motion
    # Its two rides: from its last keyframe at one end to its first at the other.
    one, other = stands
    rides = ((other[1] - one[2]) % whole, (one[1] - other[2]) % whole)
    return low, high, round(max(rides) / 1000, 3), round(whole / 1000, 3)


def lift_keys(master=MASTER):
    """The master's lifts: {key: (continent, x, y)}, the lower end of each as its newest path has it."""
    found = {}
    if not master.exists():
        return found
    for text in open(master, encoding="utf-8"):
        line = json.loads(text)
        key, path = line.get("key"), line.get("path")
        if isinstance(key, int) and LIFTS < key < LIFTS * 2 and path:
            found[key] = (path[0].get("map"), path[0]["x"], path[0]["y"])
    return found


def lifts(cars, motions, kept, placer=None):
    """The lifts' lines: [(key, fields)] of the cars ([(object, continent, x, y, z)], in order) the client moves as
    lifts (motions: {object: its TransportAnimation rows}), each with the key of the master's lift at its place (kept:
    lift_keys) or the next new one; and the cars left out ([(object, why)])."""
    lines, left, used = [], [], set()
    for car, continent, x, y, z in cars:
        motion = lift(motions.get(car, ()))
        if not motion:
            left.append((car, "the client does not move it as a lift" if motions.get(car) else "no motion in the client"))
            continue
        low, high, time, wait = motion
        key = next((key for key, (world, kx, ky) in sorted(kept.items()) if key not in used and world == continent
                    and math.hypot(kx - x, ky - y) <= HERE), None)
        if key is None:
            key = max([LIFTS, *kept, *used]) + 1
        used.add(key)
        fields = {"kind": "lift", "length": round(high - low, 1), "time": time, "wait": wait,
                  "path": [{"x": x, "y": y, "map": continent, "z": round(z + low, 3)},
                           {"x": x, "y": y, "z": round(z + high, 3)}]}
        if placer:
            lower, upper = placer.place(continent, x, y, z + low), placer.place(continent, x, y, z + high)
            if lower:
                fields["from"] = lower
            if upper:
                fields["to"] = upper
        lines.append((key, fields))
    return lines, left


def portals(rows, triggers, placer=None):
    """The portals' lines: [(key, fields)] of a batch's portals ([(trigger, continent, x, y, z)], in order), each from
    the client's area trigger (triggers: {ID: its AreaTrigger row}); and those left out ([(trigger, why)])."""
    lines, left = [], []
    for trigger, continent, x, y, z in rows:
        row = triggers.get(trigger)
        if not row:
            left.append((trigger, "the client has no such trigger"))
            continue
        if int(row["ContinentID"]) != continent:
            left.append((trigger, "the client has it on another continent"))
            continue
        tx, ty, tz = float(row["Pos[0]"]), float(row["Pos[1]"]), float(row["Pos[2]"])
        fields = {"kind": "portal", "length": round(math.dist((tx, ty, tz), (x, y, z)), 1),
                  "path": [{"x": tx, "y": ty, "map": continent, "z": tz}, {"x": x, "y": y, "z": z}]}
        if placer:
            into, out = placer.place(continent, tx, ty, tz), placer.place(continent, x, y, z)
            if into:
                fields["from"] = into
            if out:
                fields["to"] = out
        lines.append((PORTALS + trigger, fields))
    return lines, left


def portal_places(path):
    """The portals of a batch's places file: [(trigger, continent, x, y, z)], in the file's order."""
    return [(int(row["trigger"]), int(row["continent"]), float(row["x"]), float(row["y"]), float(row["z"]))
            for row in csv.DictReader(open(path, encoding="utf-8"))]


def lift_places(path):
    """The cars of a batch's places file: [(object, continent, x, y, z)], in the file's order."""
    return [(int(row["object"]), int(row["continent"]), float(row["x"]), float(row["y"]), float(row["z"]))
            for row in csv.DictReader(open(path, encoding="utf-8"))]


def main():
    args = sys.argv[1:]
    batches = {}
    for option in ("--lifts", "--portals"):
        if option in args:
            at = args.index(option)
            if len(args) < at + 3 or not args[at + 2].isdigit():
                print(__doc__.strip().splitlines()[-1], file=sys.stderr)
                return 2
            batches[option] = (Path(args[at + 1]), int(args[at + 2]))
            del args[at:at + 3]
    if len(args) != 2:
        print(__doc__.strip().splitlines()[-1], file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    folder = Path(args[0])
    placer = map_data().Placer(folder, Path(args[1]))
    nodes = {int(row["ID"]): row for row in table(folder, "TaxiNodes")}
    points = {}
    for row in table(folder, "TaxiPathNode"):
        points.setdefault(int(row["PathID"]), []).append(row)
    lines, left, transports = [], 0, {}
    for row in table(folder, "TaxiPath"):
        key = int(row["ID"])
        a, b = nodes.get(int(row["FromTaxiNode"])), nodes.get(int(row["ToTaxiNode"]))
        path = sorted(points.get(key, []), key=lambda p: int(p["NodeIndex"]))
        fields = flight(key, row, a, b, path) if a and b else None
        if fields:
            lines.append((key, fields))
        elif len(docks(path)) >= 2:
            transports[key] = path
        else:
            left += 1
    gone = replaced({key: docks(path) for key, path in transports.items()})
    for key, path in transports.items():
        if key in gone:
            left += 1
        else:
            lines.append((key, transport(path, placer, nodes)))
    trams = tram(folder, placer, nodes)
    if trams:
        lines.append((TRAM_KEY, trams))
    sources = {}
    if "--lifts" in batches:
        places, batch = batches["--lifts"]
        motions = {}
        for row in table(folder, "TransportAnimation"):
            motions.setdefault(int(row["TransportID"]), []).append(row)
        found, dropped = lifts(lift_places(places), motions, lift_keys(), placer)
        for car, why in dropped:
            print(f"left out: the lift car {car}: {why}")
        lines += found
        sources.update({key: batch for key, _ in found})
    gates = 0
    if "--portals" in batches:
        places, batch = batches["--portals"]
        triggers = {int(row["ID"]): row for row in table(folder, "AreaTrigger")}
        found, dropped = portals(portal_places(places), triggers, placer)
        for trigger, why in dropped:
            print(f"left out: the portal at trigger {trigger}: {why}")
        lines += found
        sources.update({key: batch for key, _ in found})
        gates = len(found)
    lines.sort(key=lambda line: line[0])
    STAGING.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    with open(STAGING, "w", encoding="utf-8") as out:
        for key, fields in lines:
            line = {"set": "Travel", "key": key, "game": "forever", "build": BUILD, "src": sources.get(key, "game"),
                    "fields": fields}
            out.write(json.dumps(line, separators=(",", ":")) + "\n")
    ships = sum(1 for _, fields in lines if fields["kind"] in ("boat", "zeppelin"))
    placed = sum(len(fields.get("docks", ())) for _, fields in lines)
    flights = sum(1 for _, fields in lines if fields["kind"] == "flight")
    print(f"Wrote {STAGING.relative_to(ROOT)}: {flights} flights, {ships} boats and zeppelins, "
          f"{'the tram' if trams else 'no tram'}, with {placed} docks on the zone maps, {len(sources) - gates} lifts, "
          f"{gates} portals "
          f"({left} ways left out; replaced: {', '.join(map(str, sorted(gone))) or 'none'}).")
    return 0


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
